-You did?

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.567
-I have the app.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.133
-You have the --
You uploaded everything?

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.400
Oh, my gosh,
look at how good you look.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.801
Come on.
Are you kidding me?

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:16.934
You are unbelievable.
You are unbelievable.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.601
Welcome back to the show
as always.

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.501
-These are cool.
-They're pretty fun, right?

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.100
-Yeah.
-Martha Stewart,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.701
we have things to talk about.
-Yes, we do.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.701
-Did you say hi to Bradley?
-I did.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.400
I took a picture with him.
-You did?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.234
-Yeah. And he looks --
-Lucky him.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.767
-I watched the movie.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.267
Well, you knew
Leonard Bernstein.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.033
-I knew the real Lenny.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.367
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.534
-How did you know Lenny?

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:40.601
--Well, he lived in Fairfield
on the weekends,

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:42.701
and he also lived
right here in New York.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.534
And I visited his apartment,

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:48.968
and we used to go
on Sunday afternoons for tea.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:49.901
-What?!
-Yeah.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.968
And his kids lived in Westport.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.567
-And what was he like?
-Oh, the maestro.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:55.501
-Yeah, he really is.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:56.734
-Yeah.
-He's fantastic.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.968
-He might have been
a little handsomer than...

00:00:58.968 --> 00:00:59.901
-Than Bradley Cooper.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.868
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.634
That's what people say
about me all the time.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.934
Oh, my God.
Just on the street they go,

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.734
"Hey, Bradley."
I go, "No, it's me, Jimmy."

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.400
-He was intense
like the Lenny in the movie.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.968
Oh, boy, was --
Bradley is so amazing.

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:15.033
-I don't know how he does
all this stuff.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.834
But you must
go to so many parties.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.601
I mean, I know you throw
dinner parties, but you must --

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.434
I mean, attend a lot of parties.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:22.968
-I go to a lot of
dinner parties,

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.334
and I go -- but I do have
a lot of dinner parties, too.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:28.200
I have a table that seats
18 in my dining room,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.901
and so I like
to fill it because --

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.467
And I live in a place --
you know,

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:35.200
I live in Bedford and Bedford
is like Beverly Hills.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.767
I mean, there's so many movie
stars hanging out there now.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.734
They're all moving to Bedford
for some reason.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.200
-It's a happening place.
-Yeah. Happening.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.968
And they're fun. They're fun.

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:46.601
I had Michael Kelly over
and I was a little scared of him

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.033
because he's played
pretty evil guys, you know?

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.434
-Oh, yeah.
But no. How was he?

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.634
-He was nice.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:53.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.567
-He was okay.
-Yeah.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:56.801
You know, I've talked to people

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.734
that have had dinner
at your house

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.968
and they, they go --
I go, "How was it?"

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.300
And they go, "She's really fun."

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.701
-Oh, they did say that?
-Yeah.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.133
-Like who?

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.033
-And I go, "What do you mean?
Of course she's really fun."

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.734
-I try to be fun.
-You are fun.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.067
But maybe people go in thinking

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.300
that you're going to yell
at them or something.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.534
-No. Why?
I don't yell at people.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.534
-Have you ever yelled
at anyone at a dinner party?

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.334
-At my guests? No!

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.100
-"Hey, elbows off the table!"

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.534
-No, except
for the fire department

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:23.968
that came during one
very important dinner party

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.400
and some alarm went off
in my house someplace,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.267
and the fire department
comes in with all the tools,

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:31.334
you know, the axes
and the hoses and everything.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:32.567
And they tell everybody
to get out.

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.901
And it was like 20 degrees
below zero outside.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:37.067
-And you're like, "Excuse me,
this is Snoop Dogg.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.334
He's allowed to do this."
Yeah.

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:39.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.100
-And then, oh, Snoop Dogg,
talk about Snoop Dogg.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.167
He came to dinner.
And, you know,

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:47.467
he said, "I'll be there --
About three guys, three guys.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.567
We're just getting off the plane
and we have to go to New York.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:52.434
But he'll stop by."
So I said, "Come for lunch."

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:56.033
And he came and seven bodyguards

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.100
and they're called
Teeny and Tiny

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.100
and they're all about
seven feet tall.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.033
And they ate everything.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.300
They ate everything
and left nothing

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.000
for the rest of the guests.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.734
-Yeah. He constantly
has the munchies.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.334
-I had to make peanut butter
and jelly sandwiches

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:13.701
for my friends, you know.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.067
Oh, my God, it was so --
-But you have

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.934
such a good relationship,
you and --

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:21.000
-Oh, he's great. Snoop is just
like my little brother.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.133
-Yeah.
-I had three brothers,

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.267
but he was like the third --
he was like the fourth brother.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.534
-Yeah.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:29.467
Can we talk
about your shopping thing

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.300
